# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Mortgage Work — configuration (TEMPLATE)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. config.py reads `.env`; this
# template is the only one tracked in git. Never commit the real `.env`.
#
# Runtime config for the desktop app only — non-secret, the only file a
# release build may ship (the PyInstaller spec whitelists exactly these
# keys when bundling .env). Infrastructure credentials arrive with the
# login session (see the "Client service entitlement" section in
# server/.env.example); the data-store viewers (browser/) are a standalone
# unit with their own browser/.env.example.

# Auth service — where this desktop app reaches email-code login. Local dev
# runs server/ on this box; a deployment points at the hosted instance.
AUTH_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9898

# Local agent service port (chat over WebSocket, spawned by app.py).
# 19786–19791 is the browser/ viewer block (may grow upward) — keep clear.
AGENT_PORT=19860
